+# Approved Transport Usage
+
+<a id="claim-approved-transport-usage"></a>
+### Claim: approved-transport-usage
+
+- **Kind:** derived
+- **State:** current
+- **Statement:** The approved transport comparison is HTTP with JSON for public client integrations, while gRPC is permitted only for internal high-throughput services when both endpoints are controlled by the team.
+- **Derived from:**
+  - [transport-public-http-json](../topics/transport.md#claim-transport-public-http-json)
+  - [transport-internal-controlled-grpc](../topics/transport.md#claim-transport-internal-controlled-grpc)
+- **Evidence:**
+  - **Source:** [Architecture v1](../../sources/architecture-v1.md)
+  - **Locator:** heading "Public transport", lines 5-8
+  - **Source:** [Architecture v2](../../sources/architecture-v2.md)
+  - **Locator:** heading "Approved decision", lines 5-12
+
+## Limitations
+
+- The internal gRPC statement is a conditional permission, not a requirement to use
+  gRPC for every internal service.
+- The historical [gRPC-default recommendation](../topics/transport.md#claim-transport-grpc-default-recommendation)
+  remains visible as superseded and retains its contradiction relation with the
+  public HTTP claim.
+- This comparison does not establish file-upload size limits or retention policies;
+  the available operational source does not define them.
